---
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import ScrollTable from '../../components/ScrollTable.astro';
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { INSTALL } from '../../data/site';

const layers = [
  {
    layer: 'CSS classes',
    pkg: '@kyralabs/m3e-css',
    when: 'Static components: buttons, cards, lists, chips, text fields, app bars. No JavaScript.',
  },
  {
    layer: 'Custom elements',
    pkg: '@kyralabs/m3e-elements',
    when: 'Behavior without a framework: menus, dialogs, sheets, pickers, springs and shape morphs. Zero dependencies, one entry per element.',
  },
  {
    layer: 'React',
    pkg: '@kyralabs/m3e-react',
    when: 'React apps: React Aria for behavior and accessibility, Motion for springs.',
  },
  {
    layer: 'Tokens',
    pkg: '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens',
    when: 'Always: the CSS custom properties every layer reads, the fonts, Material Symbols and seed themes.',
  },
];
---

<Guide
  title="Get started"
  description="Install one package, load one stylesheet, then use whichever layer fits your stack: CSS classes, custom elements or React."
>
  <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
  <p>
    The umbrella package <code>@kyralabs/m3exp-web</code> re-exports every layer. Add
    <code>@kyralabs/m3e-tokens</code> as well so your package manager lets you import its icon
    stylesheets by path (pnpm only resolves direct dependencies).
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={INSTALL} lang="sh" label="install command" />

  <h2 id="layers">Pick a layer</h2>
  <p>
    The three component layers render the same DOM with the same classes, so they share one theme
    and mix on one page: a static card from CSS classes, a menu element inside it, a React date
    picker next to it.
  </p>
  <ScrollTable label="Layers">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Layer</th><th scope="col">Package</th><th scope="col">Use it for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          layers.map((l) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{l.layer}</th>
              <td><code>{l.pkg}</code></td>
              <td>{l.when}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ScrollTable>

  <h2 id="css">Load the CSS</h2>
  <p>
    One import gives you the fonts, the tokens, the baseline theme and every component class. Icons
    are a separate stylesheet because the Material Symbols font is large.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="css"
    label="CSS imports"
    code={`@import '@kyralabs/m3exp-web/css/index.css'; /* fonts, tokens, baseline theme, every class */
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/material-symbols.css'; /* icons */`}
  />
  <p>
    To ship less CSS, import the token stylesheets and only the components a page shows; each
    component file also works on its own:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="css"
    label="per-component CSS imports"
    code={`@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/fonts.css';
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/tokens.css';
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-tokens/theme.css';
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-css/icon.css';
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-css/button.css';
@import '@kyralabs/m3e-css/card.css';`}
  />

  <h2 id="first-component">Your first component</h2>
  <p>The same button in each layer:</p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="html"
    label="CSS class example"
    code={`<!-- CSS classes: no JavaScript -->
<button type="button" class="m3e-button m3e-button--filled m3e-button--size-m">
  <span class="m3e-icon" aria-hidden="true">save</span>
  Save
</button>`}
  />
  <CodeBlock
    lang="tsx"
    label="React example"
    code={`import { Button, Icon } from '@kyralabs/m3exp-web/react';

<Button variant="filled" size="m" icon={<Icon name="save" />} onPress={save}>
  Save
</Button>`}
  />
  <p>
    The button has no custom element: CSS draws it completely, and React adds the press morph on a
    spring. Components whose behavior CSS cannot provide, such as menus, have an element:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="html"
    label="custom element example"
    code={`<button id="more" type="button" class="m3e-icon-button" aria-label="More options">
  <span class="m3e-icon" aria-hidden="true">more_vert</span>
</button>
<m3e-menu anchor="more">
  <m3e-menu-item value="edit" icon="edit">Edit</m3e-menu-item>
  <m3e-menu-item value="share" icon="share">Share</m3e-menu-item>
</m3e-menu>

<script type="module">
  import '@kyralabs/m3exp-web/elements'; // registers every element
</script>`}
  />
  <p>
    <code>@kyralabs/m3exp-web/elements</code> registers every element. To load only the ones a page
    uses, install <code>@kyralabs/m3e-elements</code> and import its per-element entries, such as
    <code>@kyralabs/m3e-elements/menu.js</code>; the <a href="/get-started/astro/">Astro guide</a>
    shows how.
  </p>

  <h2 id="next">Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Set up a project: <a href="/get-started/react/">React with Vite</a>, <a href="/get-started/astro/">Astro</a> or <a href="/get-started/html/">plain HTML</a>.</li>
    <li>Choose a font profile and ship only the icons you use: <a href="/get-started/fonts-and-icons/">fonts and icons</a>.</li>
    <li>Generate a theme from your brand color: <a href="/get-started/theming/">theming</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</Guide>
